    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d926">

                <pb facs="0724" n="608" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg608"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13367.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Special Agent Canova to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Zacatecas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-02">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 2, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The convention of generals<anchor n="65" xml:id="d926-f1"/> which met in Mexico
                    City yesterday will adjourn to hold an open caucus in Aguascalientes beginning
                    on the 5th and lasting until the 10th, when the convention will be called to
                    order and will terminate its work in Aguascalientes.</p>
                <p>A telegram received here today by Governor Acuña Navarro from General Lucio
                    Blanco, who signed as secretary of a committee of fifty-eight generals, gives
                    this information, and states that the First Chief has expressed his entire
                    conformity with this program and his willingness to abide by the decision of the
                    convention.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canova</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d926-f1" n="65" xml:id="d926-f1-content">
                <p>See Mr. Belt’s telegram of September 29, paragraph 3.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
